22 + 10 + (6 * 9) + (2 * 6) = 22 + 10 + 54 + 12 = 98 \boxed{98}
Janet starts with 22 green pens and 10 yellow pens. That's a total of 22 + 10 = 32 pens.

She buys 6 bags of blue pens, where each bag has 9 pens.  So she gets 6 * 9 = 54 blue pens.

She also buys 2 bags of red pens, where each bag has 6 pens.  So she gets 2 * 6 = 12 red pens.

In total, she has 32 + 54 + 12 = 98 pens.

\boxed{98}

